import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Lodestra Privacy Policy - Made With Pixels, LLC"
  description="Privacy Policy for Lodestra, the trip organizer for Android"
  heading="Lodestra Privacy Policy"
  updated="October 2026"
  footerLinks={[{ href: '/lodestra', label: 'About Lodestra' }]}
>
  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Lodestra is a trip organizer for Android made by Made With Pixels, LLC. Lodestra has no servers of its own: your trips stay on your device and in your own Google Drive.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Information on Your Device</h2>
    <p>
      The trips, itinerary items and notes you enter are stored in a database on your device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Google Sign-In and Google Drive</h2>
    <p>
      If you turn on backup, Lodestra asks you to sign in with Google and to allow access to Google Drive. It uses two limited permissions:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>App data folder</strong> (<code>drive.appdata</code>): a hidden folder in your Drive that only Lodestra can see, used for backups and app settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Files Lodestra creates or you open with it</strong> (<code>drive.file</code>): Lodestra can only see files it created or that you chose to open with it. It cannot see the rest of your Drive.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This data goes directly between your device and Google; we never receive it. Google's handling of it is covered by the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>. Lodestra's use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Sharing a Trip</h2>
    <p>
      When you share a trip, Lodestra uses Google Drive to give the people you choose access to that trip's file, as a viewer or an editor. Their email address is used only to grant that access. The invite link you send contains the trip's name and your display name, which anyone you send it to can read. The link alone does not give access to the trip.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What We Don't Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't sell your information or share it with data brokers.</li>
      <li>We don't use your Google Drive data for advertising.</li>
      <li>We don't send your trips to any server of ours.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

